NWFPE for riscose
=================

NWFPE, the NetWinder Floating Point Emulator (Scott Bambrough, Rebel.com,
1998-1999, on John Hauser's SoftFloat), emulates the FPA: the floating
point instructions (coprocessors 1 and 2) that Acorn C and other RISC OS
compilers generate, which RISC OS carries out with its FPEmulator module.

The files are those of the Linux kernel's arch/arm/nwfpe, as of commit
47ba5f39eab3c2a9a1ba878159a6050f2bbfc0e2 (17 May 2023), unchanged, except:

  fpmodule.c, fpmodule.inl
          riscose's own versions of NWFPE's port layer (the kernel's
          module glue and pt_regs access): one FPA, set up by
          riscose_fpe_init(); registers, flags and memory reached through
          src/armul/arm.c; a trapped exception reported there rather than
          sent as SIGFPE.
  compat/ the few kernel headers the other files include (thread state,
          get_user/put_user, do_div).
  softfloat-macros
          shift64RightJamming's two ARM assembler comment markers
          (__asm__("@...")) are kept to ARM hosts (#ifdef __arm__): other
          hosts' assemblers reject them.

Not taken: entry.S and the kernel's Makefile.

src/armul/armsupp.c hands coprocessor 1 and 2 instructions to
ARMul_FPEInstr() (src/armul/arm.c), which calls NWFPE's EmulateAll(); NWFPE
does the instruction's memory accesses and base write-back itself.
Extended precision is on (CONFIG_FPE_NWFPE_XP). Not emulated, as in NWFPE:
packed decimal (LDFP/STFP) and trapped exceptions' delivery to the program.

NWFPE is GPL-2.0-or-later; SoftFloat (softfloat*, milieu.h, ARM-gcc.h)
carries its own notice, in those files.
